From 12003ab51a318d40435f3a257902aa19b2b85a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:32:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs(help): write the missing how-tos and give article
 sections stable anchors

New articles for features that shipped without a how-to:
- getting-started: install-and-pair, browser-import
- desktop-app: desktop-app-overview, replay-folders
- analyzer: today, opponents, strategies, trends, macro, maps, builds,
  replays, arcade, reading-the-charts (each covers what the section
  answers, how to drill in and how much data it needs)
- game-page: game-page, game-page-replay, game-page-accurate-playback
- opponents: opponent-dossier
- builds: practice-ghost-build, randomizer
- account-data: delete-account, public-profile, player-channels
- stream-studio: voice, obs-auto-scene-switching (links to the
  Stream Studio crash course rather than copying it)
- troubleshooting: my-game-didnt-show-up

Existing articles: "Dashboard & analyzer" becomes the section index and
drops the map-veto claim; Filters gains patch-preset and too-short
sections; the OBS step says the overlay token is created for you;
Getting started links the install guide. Articles that explain stats
say every number is computed with fixed rules, never AI.

Headings take an optional `anchor`, rendered as an id on /help/<slug>
so later info tips can link to one section (helpAnchorPath,
helpArticleAnchors). lib/glossary.ts seeds Pulse ID, toon, Net MMR,
verified pairs, MMR impact, Group same player and barcode, each linked
to its article section.

Tests: every analyzer section has its article, every HelpLink /
LazyHelpLink / helpSlug in the source resolves, anchors are unique and
links to /help/<slug>#<anchor> resolve, glossary links resolve. Search
expectations follow the new dedicated articles.

