From cb81496cd0487f91e84452592c301d959190b75e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:32:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(web): analyzer sections open with a header and a
 "How to read this" link

components/analyzer/SectionHeader.tsx, rendered by SectionPanel and
OpponentsRoute, shows the section's name, its tabs.ts intro, a "How to
read this" link that opens the section's help article in the side
sheet (/app/maps -> /help/maps), and an actions slot.

- The title is an h2: the context bar stays the page's h1.
- "Hide intro" hides the intro for that section on this device
  (localStorage analyzer.intro.hidden.<tabId>) and moves focus to the
  help link; following "How to read this" brings the intro back.
- PageHeader gains `as` ("h1" | "h2"), a smaller "section" size and a
  description id; existing pages render exactly as before.
- HelpLink and LazyHelpLink take an optional onOpen, called whenever
  the reader follows the link (sheet or new tab).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KG8e5a59qtUDJJY3Fm1hxC
